If you are setting up your own topologies from scratch in Packet Tracer, build these three master labs to cover most (about 70-90 percent) of the tested exam CLI:

Lab A (The Switching & L2 Block): Build a 3-switch topology. Create VLANs 10, 20, 30. Configure 802.1Q trunks, 
an LACP EtherChannel between two switches, set up Rapid PVST+ with a forced Root Bridge, and enable BPDU Guard on all access ports.  


​Lab B (The Routing & Edge Block): Connect a Layer 3 switch to a router using Router-on-a-Stick (ROAS) or SVIs.
Run single-area OSPFv2 between the router and an edge router. Configure a floating static route as a backup ISP path.  


​Lab C (The Services & Security Block): On your edge router, configure a DHCP pool with excluded addresses, set up Dynamic PAT (NAT Overload) for outbound internet traffic,
and apply an Extended ACL on the LAN interface to block HTTP traffic from VLAN 10 while allowing it from VLAN 20. 
